<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Khunan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1221">1221</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Khunan · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasions-of-georgia">Mongol invasions of Georgia</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Khunan was fought in 1221 in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, where the Mongol vanguard led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebe">Jebe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a> defeated the Georgian army of King George IV. It was the first Mongol attack on Georgia, part of a long reconnaissance raid around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. The unexpected defeat broke the kingdom's military confidence, and it was followed by Khwarazmian and later full Mongol invasions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-khunan.jpg" alt="Battle of Khunan" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nika Khoperia (translation by Ercwlff) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mongol_invasion_of_Georgia-en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
